--  Anatomy layout (local Y):
--   -60 to -50   Pommel — large circular eye-socket (ring + filled disc + pupil)
--   -50 to -42   Grip    — short wrapped column, narrowing wrap ridges
--   -42 to -38   Crossguard center block
--   -38 to -22   Horn zone — two swept bezier arcs + inner downward fangs
--   -22 to -14   Ricasso — full-width unsharpened shoulder
--   -14 to  28   Forte   — broad blade body, slow taper, with fuller groove
--    28 to  44   Center  — mid-blade, taper continues
--    44 to  54   Foible  — upper third, narrowing
--    44 to  56   False edge — secondary bevel cluster on +Z face
--    54 to  58   Point   — fast convergence
--    58 to  60   Tip     — terminal cluster
